    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nNestled on the outskirts of the highly sought-after coastal town of Skerries, this charming three-bedroom semi-detached cottage presents a wonderful opportunity to acquire a home with exceptional potential on a generous site.\n\nOccupying a large plot with extensive gardens, the property offers excellent scope for extension and further development, subject to the necessary planning permissions. A wide side entrance provides convenient vehicular access to the rear, enhancing the property's versatility and future possibilities.\n\nThe accommodation is well laid out and comprises an entrance hall, a comfortable living room featuring an open fireplace, three bedrooms, a shower room, and a kitchen. To the rear, a private courtyard is complemented by a range of useful block-built outbuildings. Beyond the courtyard lies a substantial lawned garden bordered by mature hedging, creating a private and tranquil outdoor setting.\n\nIdeally positioned within walking distance of Skerries town centre and situated on a regular bus route, the property enjoys the perfect balance of peaceful surroundings and everyday convenience.\n\nSkerries is renowned as one of North County Dublin's most desirable seaside towns, offering an exceptional quality of life with an abundance of amenities. Residents enjoy a wide selection of cafés, restaurants, shops, and excellent primary and secondary schools. The town boasts beautiful beaches, scenic coastal walks, and an impressive range of sporting facilities including football, rugby, sailing, golf, cricket, and GAA clubs.\n\nCommuters are particularly well catered for, with regular rail and bus services providing easy access to Dublin City Centre and beyond. In addition, the M1 and M50 motorways, together with Dublin Airport, are all within approximately 15 minutes' drive.\n\nThis is a rare opportunity to acquire a character-filled home on a substantial site in a prime location, offering outstanding potential for future enhancement."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntrance Hall - \nCarpet to floor\n\nLiving Room - \nWood floor, coving, feature fireplace with open insert\n\nBedroom 1 - \nWood floor, coving, over looking front garden\n\nBedroom 2 - \nWood floor, over looking rear courtyard\n\nBedroom 3 - \nCarpet to floor, coving, over looking rear courtyard\n\nKitchen - \nTiled floor, floor and wall mounted units, tiled splash back, plumbed for washing machine, door to rear garden\n\nShower Room - \nTiled floor, part tiled walls, shower unit, WC, WHB, window\n\nRear Garden - \nLarge rear garden with vehicle access to the side, mainly in lawn, block built storage sheds\n\nFront Garden - \nPrivate front garden, pedestrian access, lawn area with mature planting, vehicle access to the side\n\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li> Charming three-bedroom semi-detached cottage</li><li> Large site with excellent potential to extend (s.to p. p.)</li><li> Wide side access with vehicular access to the rear</li><li> Living room with open fireplace</li><li> Rear courtyard with block-built outbuildings</li><li> Walking distance to Skerries town centre</li><li> Located on a regular bus route</li><li> Easy access to Dublin City Centre, Dublin Airport, M1 and M50</ul>"
